Entailment on V, Scott's clauses (3) through (6), is generated by seven clauses. Every finite set entails bottom. A set entails top when top belongs to it, or when both its left and right pair projections entail top. A set entails a left pair when top belongs to it, or when its left projection entails the inner token. A set entails a right pair when top belongs to it, or when its right projection entails the inner token.
